"I\u0027ll start with the file named in the stack trace and the repository layout.The stack points at the repository constructor, which reads the CSV at startup, and the path is relative. I\u0027ll check whether the data file is tracked in git and whether the GetOrder code is involved.I\u0027ve read the code and the data file. The crash is a missing file at startup, not a bug in the get-order method.The cause is in \u0060OrderService.OrderRepository\u0060 constructor, \u0060src/OrderService/Orders.cs\u0060 line 22, which calls \u0060File.ReadLines(csvPath)\u0060. It\u0027s called from \u0060Program.cs\u0060 line 8 with the relative path \u0060\u0022data/orders.csv\u0022\u0060. I reported it as **hosting**, with **high** confidence.\n\n- **Why it\u0027s not the get-order code:** the repository is built once at startup, before any request. The exception is raised there, so \u0060GetOrder.cs\u0060 never runs for this error.\n- **The path:** the code doesn\u0027t set an absolute path. \u0060\u0022data/orders.csv\u0022\u0060 resolves against the working directory, so the deployed service looked for it in the wrong place and didn\u0027t find it under \u0060/app\u0060.\n- **The data file:** \u0060data/orders.csv\u0060 exists in the repo, tracked since commit \u0060916d807f5\u0060. So the file is present in source, and the problem is that the deploy didn\u0027t put it where the service looks.\n- **What I couldn\u0027t check:** the deploy configuration and the running container\u0027s working directory. \u0060GetStatus\u0060 timed out, so I didn\u0027t re-check the working-tree state.\n\nUnder the runbook, a missing data file or a deployment location problem is a **hand-off to ops**.\n\nThere is also a separate latent bug, not the cause of this error. \u0060GetOrder\u0060 reads \u0060order.Items[0].Sku\u0060 unguarded, so an order with no items would throw an index-out-of-range exception instead of returning \u00220 item(s)\u0022 with no first SKU. The runbook\u0027s auto-fix rule covers that case, so it\u0027s worth a separate case if it hasn\u0027t been raised already.\n\n[Answered by triage.investigator, did: SearchWorkspace: demos/louis-agent/samples/order-service/tests/OrderService.Tests/OrderApiTests.\u2026; ListDirectoryTree: Directory tree for demos/louis-agent/samples/order-service (depth: 3):; ReadWorkspaceFile: using System.Globalization;; ReadWorkspaceFile: using System.Globalization;; FindFiles: Found 22 file(s) matching \u0027*.cs\u0027:; FileHistory: 916d807f5  2026-11-08  Louis Marais  feat(f106.3.1): step 1 - the order-service\u2026; ReadWorkspaceFile: namespace OrderService;; ReadWorkspaceFile: namespace OrderService;; GetStatus: [Timeout] Git command exceeded 30s limit.; ReportInvestigation: Recorded step 2 of run eval-get-order-1001-20261126-225452-triage-1: The invest\u2026]"